  <text>
    <body>
      <p>The former Myer Despatch Buildings are on the corner of Barry Street and Queensberry Street. Built during the interwar period and designed by H. W. &amp; F. B. Tompkins, they are a testament to Myer's growing business, and to interwar styles of commercial architecture. The southern building is of 1920s red brick and render construction with classical detailing, while the northern exemplifies the Moderne style.</p>
